Thank you, Ruth. Annex 2 is updated with the three sub-processors.

On the ERP vendor: that is a customer instruction, not a sub-processor of Tessera's, so it does not belong in the DPA. Documenting it in the ticket with the date and the name of the person who gave the instruction is sufficient; I would also suggest a one-line confirmation email to Coastline so it is in writing on their side.

The revised draft is attached (Coastline_Tessera_DPA_v2_2026-03-09.docx). Nothing further is needed from Avery on this.

